                <head>357. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On October 25, Admiral Holloway reported to the Chief of Naval Operations that
                    all United States military forces had been withdrawn from Lebanon, and that the
                    operation was “completed”. (CINCSPECOMME telegram 251221Z; National Archives and
                    Records Administration, RG 218, JCS Files) The Army Attaché in Lebanon reported
                    that the departure of the last of the U.S. troops passed quietly and without
                    incident. He noted that the “country continues calm with Beirut again a thriving
                    commercial center.” (USARMA telegram CX 357, October 28; <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >ibid.</hi>) The withdrawal of British troops from Jordan began on October
                    20, and the airlift of the main body of paratroopers from Amman began on October
                    25. (Telegram 1183 from Amman, October 24; Department of State, Central Files,
                    785.00/10–2458) The CINCSPECOMME telegram is included in <ref
                        target="frus:frus1958-60v11mSupp">the microfiche supplement</ref>.</p>
            </div>
